IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `poca-nouns`

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, sections 339ZH to 339ZL (information orders) -- LAYER 1.   Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
-- An information order is an order of a magistrates' court (or, in Scotland, the sheriff) that makes a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- or who made a disclosure, provide information.  The person who meets it is the respondent; the rules below are about when the order may be made,
-- what the respondent can be made to pay for not complying, what is done with what the respondent says, how the respondent can appeal and what the respondent
-- need not hand over.  The Secretary of State's duties about the code of practice (s 339ZL) and the rules of court (s 339ZK(5)) are machinery.
--
-- SHAPE.  A condition ("Condition 1 ... is met if ...") is a closed definition: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE.  An order is "made ... if satisfied that one of conditions 1 to 4
-- is met": a failed "if" is JUST FALSE on lawyer-reading (a) of NOTES.md.  A power of the court limited by its own wording answers NOTHING outside its limit.
-- The respondent's protection ("may not be used in evidence against the person") is a flat negative: JUST FALSE where it applies, NOTHING where an exception removes it.

§ `Sections 339ZH to 339ZL: information orders`

§§ `s 339ZH: the four conditions`

-- src:659 | (4) Condition 1 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:660 | (a) the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under this Part,
-- src:661 | (b) the respondent is the person who made the disclosure or is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:662 | (c) the information would assist in investigating whether a person is engaged in money laundering or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started, and
-- src:663 | (d) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 339ZH(4) (src:659-663)
GIVEN `the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is the person who made the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information would assist in investigating whether a person is engaged in money laundering or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(4) condition 1 is met` MEANS
        `the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under this Part`
    AND (`the respondent is the person who made the disclosure` OR `the respondent is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector`)
    AND `the information would assist in investigating whether a person is engaged in money laundering or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started`
    AND `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`

-- src:670 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), “external request” means a request made by an authority of a foreign country which has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding money laundering offence has been committed.
@ref s 339ZH(6) (src:670)
GIVEN `it is a request made by an authority of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding money laundering offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(6) the request is an external request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a request made by an authority of a foreign country` AND `the authority has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding money laundering offence has been committed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“external request” means a request made by an authority of a foreign country which has responsibility"

-- src:664 | (5) Condition 2 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:665 | (a) the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement,
-- src:666 | (b) an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure,
-- src:667 | (c) the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:668 | (d) the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure, and
-- src:669 | (e) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 339ZH(5) (src:664-669)
GIVEN `the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(5) condition 2 is met` MEANS
        `the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement`
    AND `an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure`
    AND `the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
    AND `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure`
    AND `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`

DECLARE `Court asked for an information order` IS ONE OF
    `a magistrates' court`
    `the sheriff`
    `another court`

-- src:671 | (6A) Condition 3 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:672 | (a) the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct—
-- src:673 | (i) operational analysis of information that is relevant to money laundering or suspected money laundering, or
-- src:674 | (ii) strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of money laundering, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities which have been, are being or are likely to be, exploited for the purposes of money laundering,
-- src:675 | for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering,
-- src:676 | (b) the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:677 | (c) where the application for the order is made to a magistrates’ court, the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL,
-- src:678 | (d) where the application for the order is made to the sheriff—
-- src:679 | (i) the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and
-- src:680 | (ii) the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL, and
-- src:681 | (e) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 339ZH(6A) (src:671-681)
GIVEN `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct operational analysis of information that is relevant to money laundering or suspected money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of money laundering, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities exploited for the purposes of money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the analysis is for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A `Court asked for an information order`
      `the person making the application to a magistrates' court has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to the sheriff is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(6A) condition 3 is met` MEANS
        (`the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct operational analysis of information that is relevant to money laundering or suspected money laundering` OR `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of money laundering, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities exploited for the purposes of money laundering`)
    AND `the analysis is for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering`
    AND `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
    AND (CONSIDER court
         WHEN `a magistrates' court` THEN `the person making the application to a magistrates' court has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL`
         WHEN `the sheriff` THEN `the application to the sheriff is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` AND `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL`
         WHEN `another court` THEN FALSE)
    AND `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`

-- src:682 | (6B) Condition 4 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:683 | (a) a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order,
-- src:684 | (b) an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct one or both of the following—
-- src:685 | (i) operational analysis of information that is relevant to money laundering or suspected money laundering, or
-- src:686 | (ii) strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of money laundering, or systematic deficiencies or vulnerabilities which have been, are being or are likely to be, exploited for the purposes of money laundering,
-- src:687 | and that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis,
-- src:688 | (c) the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering,
-- src:689 | (d) the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:690 | (e) where the application for the order is made to a magistrates’ court, the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL,
-- src:691 | (f) where the application for the order is made to the sheriff—
-- src:692 | (i) the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and
-- src:693 | (ii) the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL, and
-- src:694 | (g) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 339ZH(6B) (src:682-694)
GIVEN `a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct operational or strategic analysis, and that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A `Court asked for an information order`
      `the person making the application to a magistrates' court has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to the sheriff is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(6B) condition 4 is met` MEANS
        `a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order`
    AND `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct operational or strategic analysis, and that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis`
    AND `the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to money laundering`
    AND `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
    AND (CONSIDER court
         WHEN `a magistrates' court` THEN `the person making the application to a magistrates' court has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL`
         WHEN `the sheriff` THEN `the application to the sheriff is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` AND `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 339ZL`
         WHEN `another court` THEN FALSE)
    AND `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`

§§ `s 339ZH: the order, its content and its enforcement`

-- src:651 | (1) A magistrates' court or (in Scotland) the sheriff may, on an application made by a relevant person, make an information order if satisfied that one of conditions 1 to 4 is met.
@ref s 339ZH(1) (src:651)
GIVEN court IS A `Court asked for an information order`
      `the application is made by a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 1 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 2 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 3 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 4 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(1) the court may make an information order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF court EQUALS `another court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "A magistrates' court or (in Scotland) the sheriff"
        IF `the application is made by a relevant person` AND (`condition 1 is met` OR `condition 2 is met` OR `condition 3 is met` OR `condition 4 is met`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, on an application made by a relevant person, make an information order if satisfied that one of conditions 1 to 4 is met" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- src:652 | (2) The application must—
-- src:653 | (a) specify or describe the information sought under the order, and
-- src:654 | (b) specify the person from whom the information is sought (“the respondent”).
@ref s 339ZH(2) (src:652-654)
GIVEN `the application specifies or describes the information sought under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application specifies the person from whom the information is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(2) the application has the content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application specifies or describes the information sought under the order` AND `the application specifies the person from whom the information is sought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must (a) specify or describe the information sought under the order, and (b) specify the person from whom the information is sought"

-- src:655 | (3) An information order is an order requiring the respondent to provide—
-- src:656 | (a) the information specified or described in the application for the order, or
-- src:657 | (b) such other information as the court or sheriff making the order thinks appropriate,
-- src:658 | so far as the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent.
@ref s 339ZH(3) (src:655-658)
GIVEN `the information is specified or described in the application for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or sheriff making the order thinks the information appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(3) the information order requires the respondent to provide the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information is specified or described in the application for the order` OR `the court or sheriff making the order thinks the information appropriate`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An information order is an order requiring the respondent to provide (a) the information specified or described in the application ... or (b) such other information as the court or sheriff making the order thinks appropriate"
        IF `the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order requires the information "so far as the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent"

-- src:695 | (7) An information order must specify—
-- src:696 | (a) how the information required under the order is to be provided, and
-- src:697 | (b) the date by which it is to be provided.
@ref s 339ZH(7) (src:695-697)
GIVEN `the order specifies how the information required under the order is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order specifies the date by which it is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(7) the information order has the content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order specifies how the information required under the order is to be provided` AND `the order specifies the date by which it is to be provided` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An information order must specify (a) how the information required under the order is to be provided, and (b) the date by which it is to be provided"

-- src:698 | (8) If a person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates' court, the magistrates' court may order the person to pay an amount not exceeding £5,000.
@ref s 339ZH(8) (src:698)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates' court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the court orders the person to pay, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(8) the magistrates' court may order the person to pay the amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates' court` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates' court" (an 'if' not met is the text's no (rule of 2026-10-29, confirmed by the ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)))
        IF `the amount the court orders the person to pay, in pounds` AT MOST 5_000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may order the person to pay an amount not exceeding £5,000"

-- src:699 | (9) The sum mentioned in subsection (8) is to be treated as adjudged to be paid by a conviction of the court for the purposes of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980 or (as the case may be) the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/1675 (N.I. 26)).
@ref s 339ZH(9) (src:699)
GIVEN `the sum is the sum mentioned in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(9) the sum is treated as adjudged to be paid by a conviction of the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sum is the sum mentioned in subsection (8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is given to "The sum mentioned in subsection (8)"

-- s 339ZH(10) lets the Secretary of State substitute another sum by regulations: machinery (coverage table: inert, reason 2).  The figure encoded is that of the edition date.

-- src:701 | (11) Schedule 9 has effect for the purposes of this section in determining what is a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 339ZH(11) (src:701)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(11) the business is a business in the regulated sector` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` -- Schedule 9 decides; JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged

§§ `s 339ZH(12): definitions`

-- src:703 | “authorised NCA officer” means a National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of this section;
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:703)
GIVEN `the person is a National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the person is an authorised NCA officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of this section` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised NCA officer” means a National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General"

-- src:704 | “corresponding disclosure requirement” means a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part;
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:704)
GIVEN `it is a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the requirement is a corresponding disclosure requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corresponding disclosure requirement” means a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds"

-- src:705 | “corresponding money laundering offence” means an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence specified in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of section 340(11);
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:705)
GIVEN `it is an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence specified in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of section 340(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the offence is a corresponding money laundering offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence specified in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of section 340(11)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corresponding money laundering offence” means an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence"

-- src:706 | “the criminal intelligence function” has the meaning given by section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013;
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:706)
GIVEN `it has the meaning given by section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the function is the criminal intelligence function` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has the meaning given by section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is that of section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013, which is not among the sources

-- src:707 | “foreign country” means a country or territory outside the United Kingdom;
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:707)
GIVEN `it is a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the place is a foreign country` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign country” means a country or territory outside the United Kingdom"

-- src:708 | “foreign FIU” means a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force (as that Recommendation has effect from time to time);
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:708)
GIVEN `it is a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force (as that Recommendation has effect from time to time)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the body is a foreign FIU` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force (as that Recommendation has effect from time to time)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign FIU” means a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit"

-- src:709 | “relevant person” means—
-- src:710 | in the case of an application to a magistrates' court, the Director General of the National Crime Agency or any authorised NCA officer, or
-- src:711 | in the case of an application to the sheriff, a procurator fiscal.
@ref s 339ZH(12) (src:709-711)
GIVEN court IS A `Court asked for an information order`
      `the applicant is the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a procurator fiscal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZH(12) the applicant is a relevant person` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `a magistrates' court` THEN IF `the applicant is the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means in the case of an application to a magistrates' court, the Director General ... or any authorised NCA officer"
    WHEN `the sheriff` THEN IF `the applicant is a procurator fiscal` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an application to the sheriff, a procurator fiscal"
    WHEN `another court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition covers the two courts only

§§ `s 339ZL: the code of practice`

-- s 339ZL(1) to (6) and (9) are the Secretary of State's duty to make a code of practice about when the NCA applies for or asks for an information order on conditions 3 or 4,
-- the procedure for issuing and revising it, and the power to combine it with the code under section 22F of the Terrorism Act 2000: machinery of making a code
-- (coverage table: inert, reason 2).  s 339ZL(10) points to the definition in s 339ZH(12) and creates no rule (coverage table: inert, reason 1).  The two subsections that touch a person are below.

-- src:724 | (7) A failure by a person to comply with a provision of the code does not of itself make the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings.
@ref s 339ZL(7) (src:724)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a provision of the code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZL(7) the failure of itself makes the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person fails to comply with a provision of the code` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure by a person to comply with a provision of the code does not of itself make the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a failure to comply with a provision of the code

-- src:725 | (8) The code is admissible in evidence in criminal or civil proceedings and is to be taken into account by a court or tribunal in any case in which it appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant.
@ref s 339ZL(8) (src:725)
GIVEN `the proceedings are criminal or civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZL(8) the code is admissible in evidence and is to be taken into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are criminal or civil proceedings` AND `the code appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the code is "admissible in evidence in criminal or civil proceedings" and is to be taken into account where "it appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant"

§§ `s 339ZI: statements`

-- src:729 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to an information order may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings.
@ref s 339ZI(1) (src:729)
DECLARE `Perjury prosecution considered under section 339ZI(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (England and Wales)`
    `a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (Northern Ireland)`
    `a prosecution for perjury in Scotland`
    `a prosecution for another offence`

GIVEN `the statement was made by the person in response to an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception in subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZI(1) the statement may be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the statement was made by the person in response to an information order` AND `it is used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "A statement made by a person in response to an information order" being used "in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings"
        IF `an exception in subsection (2) applies` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply" removes the bar and says nothing more about admissibility
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings"

-- src:738 | (4) In subsection (2)(b) the reference to a prosecution for perjury is—
-- src:739 | (a) in the case of England and Wales, a reference to a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911;
-- src:740 | (b) in the case of Northern Ireland, a reference to a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (S.I. 1979/1714 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 339ZI(4) (src:738-740)
GIVEN prosecution IS A `Perjury prosecution considered under section 339ZI(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZI(4) the prosecution is a prosecution for perjury` MEANS
    CONSIDER prosecution
    WHEN `a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (England and Wales)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (Northern Ireland)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a prosecution for perjury in Scotland` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) and (b) name England and Wales and Northern Ireland only
    WHEN `a prosecution for another offence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference to a prosecution for perjury is ... a reference to a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911" (or Article 10 of the 1979 Order)

-- src:734 | (3) A statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c) unless—
-- src:735 | (a) evidence relating to it is adduced, or
-- src:736 | (b) a question relating to it is asked,
-- src:737 | by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution.
@ref s 339ZI(3) (src:734-737)
GIVEN `evidence relating to the statement is adduced by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question relating to the statement is asked by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZI(3) use of the statement by virtue of subsection (2)(c) is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `evidence relating to the statement is adduced by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` OR `a question relating to the statement is asked by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c) unless (a) evidence relating to it is adduced, or (b) a question relating to it is asked"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- the text's own bar: "A statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c)"

-- src:730 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:731 | (a) in the case of proceedings under this Part,
-- src:732 | (b) on a prosecution for perjury, or
-- src:733 | (c) on a prosecution for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 339ZI(2) (src:730-733)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution is a prosecution for perjury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution is for some other offence, and in giving evidence the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `use of the statement by virtue of subsection (2)(c) is barred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZI(2) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the prosecution is a prosecution for perjury` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the prosecution is for some other offence, and in giving evidence the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1)` AND (NOT `use of the statement by virtue of subsection (2)(c) is barred`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply" in three cases only; outside them subsection (1) stays as it is

§§ `s 339ZJ: appeals`

-- src:742 | (1) An appeal from a decision on an application for an information order lies to the relevant appeal court.
@ref s 339ZJ(1) (src:742)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision on an application for an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZJ(1) an appeal lies to the relevant appeal court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the decision is a decision on an application for an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal is "from a decision on an application for an information order"

-- src:743 | (2) An appeal under this section lies at the instance of any person who was a party to the proceedings on the application.
@ref s 339ZJ(2) (src:743)
GIVEN `the person was a party to the proceedings on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZJ(2) the appeal lies at the instance of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person was a party to the proceedings on the application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal lies "at the instance of any person who was a party"; the text does not say that no one else may appeal

-- src:744 | (3) The “relevant appeal court” is—
-- src:745 | (a) the Crown Court, in the case of a decision made by a magistrates' court in England and Wales;
-- src:746 | (b) a county court, in the case of a decision made by a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland;
-- src:747 | (c) the Sheriff Appeal Court, in the case of a decision made by the sheriff.
@ref s 339ZJ(3) (src:744-747)
DECLARE `Decision-maker on an information order` IS ONE OF
    `a magistrates' court in England and Wales`
    `a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland`
    `the sheriff`
    `another decision-maker`

DECLARE `Appeal court under section 339ZJ` IS ONE OF
    `the Crown Court`
    `a county court`
    `the Sheriff Appeal Court`

GIVEN decider IS A `Decision-maker on an information order`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Appeal court under section 339ZJ`
`s 339ZJ(3) the relevant appeal court` MEANS
    CONSIDER decider
    WHEN `a magistrates' court in England and Wales` THEN JUST `the Crown Court`
    WHEN `a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST `a county court`
    WHEN `the sheriff` THEN JUST `the Sheriff Appeal Court`
    WHEN `another decision-maker` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) to (c) name three decision-makers only

-- src:748 | (4) On an appeal under this section the relevant appeal court may—
-- src:749 | (a) make or (as the case may be) discharge an information order, or
-- src:750 | (b) vary the order.
@ref s 339ZJ(4) (src:748-750)
DECLARE `Thing the relevant appeal court might do` IS ONE OF
    `make an information order`
    `discharge an information order`
    `vary the order`
    `something else`

GIVEN action IS A `Thing the relevant appeal court might do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZJ(4) the relevant appeal court may do the thing on an appeal under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER action
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the relevant appeal court may (a) make or (as the case may be) discharge an information order, or (b) vary the order" does not say "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 339ZK: supplementary`

-- src:753 | (2) “Privileged information” is information which a person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court or, in Scotland, legal privilege as defined by section 412.
@ref s 339ZK(2) (src:753)
GIVEN `the person would be entitled to refuse to provide the information on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Scotland, the information is subject to legal privilege as defined by section 412` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZK(2) the information is privileged information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person would be entitled to refuse to provide the information on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` OR `in Scotland, the information is subject to legal privilege as defined by section 412` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Privileged information” is information which a person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege"

-- src:752 | (1) An information order does not confer the right to require a person to provide privileged information.
@ref s 339ZK(1) (src:752)
GIVEN `the information is privileged information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZK(1) the information order confers the right to require the person to provide the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is privileged information` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An information order does not confer the right to require a person to provide privileged information"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about privileged information only

-- src:754 | (3) Information provided in pursuance of an information order is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 339ZK(3) (src:754)
GIVEN `the information is provided in pursuance of an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZK(3) the provision is not to be taken to breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is provided in pursuance of an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is given to "Information provided in pursuance of an information order"

-- src:755 | (4) An application for an information order may be heard and determined in private.
@ref s 339ZK(4) (src:755)
GIVEN `it is an application for an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZK(4) the application may be heard and determined in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an application for an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "An application for an information order"

-- s 339ZK(5) lets rules of court make provision as to practice and procedure: machinery (coverage table: inert, reason 2).
